<title>POLAND: BOS mulls lowering planned '96 dividend.</title>
<headline>BOS mulls lowering planned '96 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Ochrony Srodowiska SA (BOS) is considering lowering its 1996 planned dividend payments of 40 percent of net profit, BOS' deputy president told the daily Parkiet in its Thursday edition.</p>
<p>&quot;We would like to allot a lower proportion of profits to that goal,&quot; Jerzy Pietrewicz was quoted as saying, referring to the amount of the bank's 51.5-million-zloty net profit last year going to dividends.</p>
<p>No one at the bank was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
